# Lane w20/lsi-tables: the 0x00104000 curve tables renamed from address labels to
# semantic ones, after wave 19 established what each table produces.
#
# Used as the NARROW EXEMPTION of the comment gate, which otherwise forbids any
# change to an existing comment:
#
#   python3 scripts/analysis/assert_comments_preserved.py --base main \
#       --rename-map wsa1/notes/w20-lsi-table-renames.map \
#       wsa1/prom_c/data_tables/tail_data_zone.s \
#       wsa1/prom_c/data_tables/voice_dsp_tables.s \
#       wsa1/prom_c/devices/dev10c_dev104_drivers.s
#
# It is hand-written because scripts/converters/sync_comments_to_renamed_labels.py
# derives only sub_* -> non-sub_* renames and takes none of these.  Every line was
# applied by whole-word substitution over the three sources above, so no assembly
# source anywhere in the tree still spells a left-hand name.
#
# The wave-19 notes -- FINDINGS-l7a1429-curve-tables.md, -parameter-names.md,
# -write-sequencing.md, HLE-GUIDE-l7a1429.md and their probes -- were left as
# written and still use the LEFT-HAND names.  This file is the index between them.
#
Const_0100_251=Dev104_Reg0100_Const_251
Curve_Exp2Decay_101=Curve_Exp2Gain_Percent_101
Curve_Exp2Decay_256=Curve_Fitting_Exp2Decay_256
